 "title": "Gradient descent towards a minimum",
 "caption": "Each step moves against the gradient: x ← x − η f′(x). With f = (x − 3)² and η = 0.25, the steps from 0 go 1.5, 2.25, 2.625, 2.8125: each halves the distance to the minimum at 3. Too large a step would overshoot and oscillate.",
 "alt": "The parabola (x − 3) squared with dots at x = 0, 1.5, 2.25, 2.625 and 2.8125 sliding down towards the minimum at 3.",
 "description": [
  "f(x) = (x − 3)², f′(x) = 2(x − 3).",
  "x₁ = 0 − 0.25 × (−6) = 1.5; x₂ = 2.25; x₃ = 2.625; x₄ = 2.8125.",
  "The distance to 3 halves each step because η f″ = 0.5."
